  "body_html": "<h1>Pure Strategy With Imperfect Information</h1>\n<p>For player $i$ in an imperfect-information extensive game, a pure strategy is a\nfunction assigning to every information set $P^i_k$ an action\n$$\n  a_i\\in A_i(P^i_k).\n$$\nA pure strategy profile again induces a unique terminal outcome, so every finite\nextensive game has an associated normal form.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[MFoGT, Section 6.3.2] Laraki, Renault, and Sorin, <em>Mathematical Foundations of Game Theory</em>. A pure strategy maps each information set to an available action.</li>\n</ul>",
  "proof_html": null,
